#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:86
msgid "Twitter / X Feeds - Complete Guide"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:89
msgid "Everything you need for an X feed: what each \"What to Show\" option needs, what is free and what needs X API credits, where to get the Bearer Token and post links, the settings, and what every error message means."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:93
msgid "1. What to Show - what each option needs"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:94
msgid "Pick it in Step 1 of the feed editor. It decides which fields you fill in and the starting design (you can still switch between the two X designs in Step 2)."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:99
#: src/page/edit_feed/edit_feed.jsx:1800
msgid "What to Show"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:100
msgid "You need"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:101
msgid "Free or paid"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:117
msgid "Your profile header (banner, picture, name, verified badge, Follow on X button, Posts / Following / Followers) with your latest posts in a scrolling list."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:120
msgid "Your latest posts as cards in a masonry grid - photos (up to 4), videos, reply / repost / like counts and a Share menu."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:123
msgid "Recent posts from anyone that use a #hashtag or contain your search words. X only searches the last 7 days."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:126
msgid "Posts you pick yourself (for example customers praising you), shown in the order you paste them, with 5 stars and a heading such as \"What our clients tweet about us\". Works for free - see section 2."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:129
msgid "A compact Profile Timeline that fits a sidebar or a narrow column."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:136
msgid "2. Free or paid? (X API credits)"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:139
msgid "X charges for reading posts through its API. There is no monthly plan any more: you buy credits in the X Developer Console and every request uses some of them (pay-per-use). Captain Social Feed itself is not charging anything - the cost is X's."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:142
msgid "Needs credits: Profile Timeline, Tweets Grid, Sidebar Widget, Hashtag Feed"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:143
msgid "These read posts through the X API, so they only work while your X developer account has credits. Without credits X answers \"credits depleted\" and the feed stays empty."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:145
msgid "Free: Testimonials"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:146
msgid "Without a token or without credits, Testimonials read your pasted posts from X's free public embed. You get the post text, links, author name, @username and date. Photos, videos, profile pictures and reply / repost / like counts are not available this way - they appear automatically once the feed has a Bearer Token with credits."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:148
msgid "What does it cost?"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:149
msgid "At the time of writing X charges about $0.005 per post read and $0.010 per profile read. Prices change - check X's pricing page:"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:151
msgid "Example: a Profile Timeline with 6 posts reads 6 posts + 1 profile ≈ $0.04 each time it refreshes. The plugin keeps the posts in its cache, so X is only asked again when the cache runs out: with a 1-hour cache that is up to 24 refreshes a day (≈ $1 a day); with a 12-hour cache only 2 (≈ $0.08 a day). Hashtag Feed always reads at least 10 posts per refresh."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:156
msgid "Keep the cost low:"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:156
msgid "raise Settings → Cache Management → API Cache Duration (12 or 24 hours), keep Max Posts small, and keep the Fallback Cache on so visitors still see the last posts if your credits run out."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:162
msgid "3. Get your Bearer Token"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:163
msgid "Only the Bearer Token is needed. Consumer Key / Secret, Access Token / Secret and OAuth 2.0 Client ID are for apps that post or log users in - the plugin does not use them."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:165
msgid "Open the X Developer Console"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:166
msgid "Sign in with the X account that should own the App (it does not have to be the account you show)."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:169
msgid "Create a Project and an App"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:170
msgid "Follow the sign-up questions, then create a Project and an App inside it. Apps outside a Project cannot read posts."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:172
msgid "Copy the Bearer Token"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:173
msgid "Open your App → \"Keys and tokens\" → \"Bearer Token\" → Generate (or Regenerate). Copy the whole token - it is long, starts with several \"A\"s and contains % characters. X shows it only once."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:175
msgid "Buy credits"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:176
msgid "In the Developer Console open Billing / Purchase credits and add credits (not needed for free Testimonials)."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:178
msgid "Paste it in the plugin"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:179
msgid "Feed editor → Step 1 → Bearer Token, then click \"Test Connection\". \"Connected successfully\" means the token works and has credits."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:184
msgid "Treat the token like a password: never share it in chats, emails or screenshots. Regenerating it makes the old one stop working - paste the new one in every feed that used it."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:190
msgid "4. Fill in the second field"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:192
msgid "@Username (Profile Timeline, Tweets Grid, Sidebar Widget)"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:193
msgid "The handle from the profile address, with or without @. For https://x.com/captaininfokit type:"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:195
msgid "The account must be public. Reposts and replies are hidden unless you turn them on in Step 3."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:197
msgid "Hashtag or Search Words (Hashtag Feed)"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:198
msgid "One word becomes a hashtag automatically (\"WordPress\" → #WordPress). Several words, quotes or X search operators are used as typed, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:201
msgid "X only returns posts from the last 7 days."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:203
msgid "Post Links (Testimonials)"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:204
msgid "Open the post on X → click the Share icon → \"Copy link\" (or copy the address bar). Paste one link per line, up to 20 for the free mode (100 with a token). x.com and twitter.com links both work; the posts show in the order you paste them."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:212
msgid "5. Designs and settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:214
msgid "Step 2 - two X designs"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:215
msgid "Profile Timeline (profile header + scrolling list) and Tweets Grid (masonry cards). X feeds only use these two; the other designs stay for the other platforms."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:217
msgid "Step 3 - X Options"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:218
msgid "Show Profile Header (Profile Timeline / Sidebar), Show Reposts (with a \"Reposted\" label and the original author), Show Replies."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:220
msgid "Step 3 - everything else"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:221
msgid "Section Title (heading above the feed), Columns (Tweets Grid), Max Posts, Show Posts (all / videos / photos / text), Click Action (open on X, popup or play inline), Dark Mode and the Styles tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:228
msgid "6. Error messages and how to fix them"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:233
msgid "Message"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:234
msgid "What to do"
msgstr ""

#: src/page/docs/twitter-bearer-token/twitter-bearer-token.jsx:249
msgid "After fixing the token or adding credits, open the feed and click \"Test Connection\" - saving the feed also refreshes its posts. Settings → Clear Cache refreshes every feed."
msgstr ""

